A||N||7||kinboyatuwo||Welding||||5||
Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||06-03-2001||09:36 PM||||Just wondering if anyone out there had welding knowledge, been a while and don't have my books near.<P>will a portable mig welder weld a 1/8 to 1/4 inch thick stainless.  I think that there are problems.  I weld steel a lot and remember something quirky about stainless steel welding, temp or something.<P>any help or advice would be great<P><BR>thanks <BR>chris<P>kinboyatuwo@yahoo.com<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||06-03-2001||10:05 PM||||You have to use staight argon not argon/co2 mix||||reg||1
Z||000002||operator64||06-03-2001||11:12 PM||||   You could probably get the 1/8 done easy enough with the portable you may be pushing it to get the 1/4 done with it depending on the size of the portable. If all else fails you could go with a stick welder if you want, you don't have to worry about buying a bottle of argon for a small project.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||kinboyatuwo||06-04-2001||12:26 PM||||Thats what i thought.  I didnt  think i used argon the last time that i did a small job.<P>thanks for all the help, any other advice would be great.<P>chris<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||06-04-2001||03:30 PM||||I've been welding 1/8 mild steel with 100 amp Mig welder. I don't think that you can do anything thicker or stainless with that amperage.<P>BTW, I'm using flux core wire, so no gas.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-04-2001||09:32 PM||||in my opinion flux cores wire sucks. I would rather go with gas anytime. You get better welds. And they certianly are neater.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jake_Dragon||06-04-2001||09:49 PM||||When appearance counts Tig is the way to go.<BR>Flux core is ok and looks better if you run it along with a shielding gas. Not all wire is the same make sure it matches what you are welding or it will color differently when polished.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroJoe||06-05-2001||09:26 AM||||Also remember that your welds arent going to be stainless either, you'll want to protect the welds or they'll rust while the rest of the metal doesnt.<P>Stainless, when heated, will also make some funky gases.  Make sure you do this outside or have really good ventilation.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
